    "invoice": "INV-2001",
    "paymentDate": "2026-09-27T03:00:00.000Z"
  }
}

docs {
  # Update a purchase

  Partial update: send only the fields to change (at least one). The server fills `updated` with an audit stamp; undeclared keys are ignored.

  ## Auth

  Bearer token of a user whose role is `ADMIN` (send **auth/Log in** first; it stores `{{token}}`).

  ## Path parameters

  | Name | Type | Required | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `id` | integer | yes | Positive integer. |

  ## Body (JSON)

  Any subset of the fields below (none is required on update).

  | Field | Type | Required | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `paymentStatus` | string | no | One of `PENDING`, `SUCCESS`, `FAILED`, `REJECTED`. |
  | `fulfillmentStatus` | string | no | One of `PENDING`, `SHIPPED`, `DELIVERED`, `CANCELLED`. |
  | `reference` | string \| null | no | Max 100 characters. |
  | `invoice` | string \| null | no | Max 100 characters. |
  | `paymentDate` | string (ISO date) \| null | no | When payment was taken. |
  | `data` | object \| null | no | Free-form metadata; the server adds `lines`. |

  ## Responses

  ### 200 OK

    {
      "message": "Purchase updated",
      "data": {
        "id": 1,
        "userId": 1,
        "reference": "WEB-1001",
        "totalAmount": "29.9",
        "taxes": "2.99",
        "discountAmount": "0",
        "finalAmount": "32.89",
        "paymentStatus": "PENDING",
        "fulfillmentStatus": "PENDING",
        "invoice": null,
        "paymentDate": null,
        "data": {
          "lines": [
            {
              "productId": 1,
              "quantity": 2,
              "unitPrice": "14.95"
            }
          ]
        },
        "user": {
          "id": 1,
          "name": "Store",
          "lastName": "Administrator",
          "email": "admin@lpaecomms.test"
        },
        "products": [
          {
            "id": 1,
            "purchaseId": 1,
            "productId": 1,
            "amount": "29.9",
            "product": {
              "id": 1,
              "name": "Wireless Ergonomic Mouse",
              "code": "wireless-ergonomic-mouse"
            }
          }
        ],
        "created": {
          "client": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
          "server": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
          "serverDate": "2026-09-27",
          "serverTime": "12:30:14",
          "unixTime": 1790476214,
          "user": 1,
          "role": "ADMIN"
        },
        "updated": {
          "client": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
          "server": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
          "serverDate": "2026-09-27",
          "serverTime": "12:30:14",
          "unixTime": 1790476214,
          "user": 1,
          "role": "ADMIN"
        },
        "statusName": "ACTIVE",
        "status": 1,
        "createdAt": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z"
      },
      "pagination": null
    }

  ### 400 Bad Request — validation failed

  `id` is invalid, the body is empty, or a field is invalid. Also returned when a referenced id does not exist.

    {
      "message": "Some fields need attention.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": [
        {
          "field": "userId",
          "message": "Invalid input"
        }
      ]
    }

  ### 401 Unauthorized — missing, invalid or expired token

    {
      "message": "Sign in to continue.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": []
    }

  ### 403 Forbidden — the token's role is not ADMIN

    {
      "message": "You do not have permission to do this.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": []
    }

  ### 404 Not Found — no active purchase with this id

  Soft-deleted records answer 404 too.

    {
      "message": "Purchase not found.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": []
    }

  Outside production, error bodies also carry `stack`.
}
